        <h2>
          <button class="faq-trigger" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">
            <span class="question-text">Why do cats knead with their paws?</span>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="details" id="faq-2">
          <p>Kneading is a comfort behavior that starts in kittenhood. Adult cats often do it when they feel relaxed, safe, or especially happy.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h2>
          <button class="faq-trigger" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">
            <span class="question-text">How much sleep do cats need?</span>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="details" id="faq-3">
          <p>Most cats sleep between 12 and 16 hours a day. Kittens and senior cats may sleep even more.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h2>
          <button class="faq-trigger" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">
            <span class="question-text">Why do cats stare at you?</span>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="details" id="faq-4">
          <p>Cats stare to read your body language, check whether you are moving, and sometimes to ask for attention or food.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h2>
          <button class="faq-trigger" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-5">
            <span class="question-text">Do indoor cats need enrichment?</span>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="details" id="faq-5">
          <p>Yes. Toys, climbing spots, scratching posts, and short play sessions help indoor cats stay healthy and mentally engaged.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
